  "unreadable": [
    "outer-top-row positions 1 and 10 (top-left and top-right outer corner pads): no callout of their own; the GND callout lines pass over them on the way to the inner corner pads."
  ],
  "uncertain": [
    "Physical layout is a 64-pad double ring (outer ring 10 pads per side, inner ring 8 per side) around a square module; split into eight single-row connectors (rows, columns excluding shared corners). The connector grouping and corner assignment are an interpretation.",
    "Pad assignment of each callout was traced by following curved leader lines in a small image; staggered inner/outer pads make the trace error-prone.",
    "Top outer corner pads may be GND (GND leader lines pass over them) but are recorded as \"?\".",
    "Peripheral function names were composed from the column header plus the printed peripheral number (e.g. \"0\" under SPI next to \"RX\" -> \"SPI0 RX\"), per the image key; ADC column number -> \"ADC0\".",
    "GP47 row (ADC7, PSRAM CSn) is drawn faded/greyed in the image; meaning not stated."
  ],
  "notes": "Image \"Pins and Dims\", RP2350B 25.4x25.4mm, 64 pins (48 GPIO). Grey/blue/green number boxes next to each pad copied as first function after the GP label."
}
